{#
One shared entry, as a line in the shared calendar's agenda.

This is where the detail is actually read — the location, the people, the note —
because a month cell has room for a title and nothing else, and on a phone not
even that. The grids say WHEN somebody is busy at a glance; this says what the
link was ticked to say about it. It was the row of the day list printed under the
month grid, and it is now the row of the agenda VIEW: the same job, reached by
the switcher rather than by scrolling past a calendar.

It carries no horizontal padding of its own, because the day body it sits in is
already inset — see calendar/_agenda_shell.html.twig, where the date used to be
a rail beside this column and is now a heading above it. Padding here would step
the times in twice on the agenda and nowhere else.

It is a `subgrid` row of that shell's grid rather than a flex line, which is
what makes its time lane the same width as every other row's in the view
including the ones the owner's own chip draws. The lane is a track and a track
is sized against its whole column; a `shrink-0` span is sized against itself.
The colour track is column two and this row leaves it empty on purpose — a
shared page says nothing about the owner's calendars, which is the rule stated
above — so the label takes columns two and three together.

The branch below is on `entry.isDetailed()` rather than on the link's settings,
and that is the load-bearing part of this file. A private event inside an
otherwise detailed link arrives here with every field null — see
ShareLinkReader, where EventPrivacy is the ceiling over the checkboxes — and
asking the LINK whether to draw a label would draw it an empty one. Asking the
ENTRY is the only question that cannot be wrong.

Nothing here may add a `title` attribute, a `data-` attribute or a JSON payload.
It has only what the DTO carries, which is the point of the DTO; the way to keep
it that way is to add nothing that would need more.

Variables:
  entry       SharedOccurrence
  zone        string
  timeFormat  string
#}
<li class="col-span-full grid grid-cols-subgrid items-baseline py-1.5
           border-t border-line first:border-t-0">
    <span class="tabular-nums text-xs font-medium text-ink-soft">
        {% if entry.isAllDay %}
            {{ 'calendar.share.all_day'|trans }}
        {% else %}
            {{ entry.startsAt|date(timeFormat, zone) }}–{{ entry.endsAt|date(timeFormat, zone) }}
        {% endif %}
    </span>

    <span class="col-span-2 min-w-0">
        {% if entry.isDetailed %}
            <span class="block truncate text-sm text-ink">
                {{ entry.title ?? 'calendar.share.busy'|trans }}
            </span>

            {% if entry.location is not null %}
                <span class="block truncate text-xs text-ink-muted">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot text-[10px] mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ entry.location }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}

            {% if entry.participants is not empty %}
                <span class="block truncate text-xs text-ink-muted">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-users text-[10px] mr-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ entry.participants|join(', ') }}
                </span>
            {% endif %}

            {% if entry.description is not null %}
                <span class="mt-1 block whitespace-pre-line text-xs text-ink-muted">{{ entry.description }}</span>
            {% endif %}
        {% else %}
            <span class="block text-sm text-ink-muted">{{ 'calendar.share.busy'|trans }}</span>
        {% endif %}
    </span>
</li>
